Snippet:
src/serve/serve_options.cpp
        } else if (arg == "--top-k") {
            const int top_k = parse_nonnegative_int(require_value("--top-k"), "top-k");
            if (top_k > 20) { throw std::invalid_argument("top-k must be in [0,20]"); }
            options.sampling_overrides.top_k = top_k;
        }

`--top-k`'s upper bound is the sampler's API limit, but the literal 20 is written twice here — in the check and in the error message — so the two can drift. Introduce one named constant for the bound and use it in both places.

Show the change as a unified diff. Be terse: the diff plus at most three sentences.
